WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.225
Lesson 10.8.

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:05.875
DeFi rates: term structure, fixed vs floating.

00:00:05.875 --> 00:00:08.082
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:11.244
able to read DeFi's interest-rate curve and position

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.690
for fixed or floating rates deliberately.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.280
Here's the plan.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.965
First, the key ideas.

00:00:17.965 --> 00:00:20.680
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.205
Then, your checklist.

00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:24.367
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:29.225
First, Floating rates: lending and borrowing APYs

00:00:29.225 --> 00:00:32.372
that change with utilisation (Module 3).

00:00:32.372 --> 00:00:35.725
Next, Fixed rates: PTs (10.1), fixed-rate

00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:39.777
lending markets and fixed-rate borrowing (#22).

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:44.392
Then, Term structure: PT implied yields across maturities

00:00:44.392 --> 00:00:48.352
form a yield curve (e.g. 3-month vs 12-month).

00:00:48.352 --> 00:00:51.004
Upward sloping: the market expects rates

00:00:51.004 --> 00:00:52.662
to stay high or rise.

00:00:52.662 --> 00:00:55.082
Inverted: it expects them to fall.

00:00:55.082 --> 00:00:58.743
Also, Positioning: buying PT = receiving a fixed

00:00:58.743 --> 00:01:01.882
rate (you win if floating rates fall).

00:01:01.882 --> 00:01:04.756
Buying YT = receiving the floating rate

00:01:04.756 --> 00:01:07.427
(you win if floating rates rise).

00:01:07.427 --> 00:01:10.183
Fixed-rate borrowing = paying a fixed rate

00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:13.047
(you win if floating borrow rates rise).

00:01:13.047 --> 00:01:16.801
And finally, Basis between venues: the same asset's rates

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:20.491
can differ across protocols and chains; the gap reflects

00:01:20.491 --> 00:01:23.857
risk, liquidity and friction as much as opportunity.

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:27.655
Let's look at the chart: PT

00:01:27.655 --> 00:01:31.167
price converges to 1.00 at maturity.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.727
Take a moment with it.

00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:35.137
It's everything we've just said, in one picture.

00:01:36.437 --> 00:01:38.952
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:38.952 --> 00:01:45.032
Stablecoin PT implied yields: 3-month 7%, 12-month 9%.

00:01:45.032 --> 00:01:47.335
You need the money in 12 months

00:01:47.335 --> 00:01:49.854
and think rates will fall: buy the

00:01:49.854 --> 00:01:51.881
12-month PT and lock 9%.

00:01:51.881 --> 00:01:54.434
If you think rates will rise instead,

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:57.188
stay floating (supply to lending) or buy

00:01:57.188 --> 00:01:59.271
YT with a small, capped amount.

00:02:00.571 --> 00:02:02.031
Here's your checklist.

00:02:02.031 --> 00:02:03.566
Do it now, for real.

00:02:03.566 --> 00:02:05.370
First, I can state whether each

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.361
position is fixed or floating.

00:02:07.361 --> 00:02:11.656
Next, I compare implied rates across maturities before locking.

00:02:11.656 --> 00:02:15.656
And finally, Maturities match my liquidity ladder (12.4).

00:02:16.956 --> 00:02:18.166
Question 1.

00:02:18.166 --> 00:02:19.318
You buy a PT. Are

00:02:19.318 --> 00:02:21.366
you receiving fixed or floating?

00:02:25.786 --> 00:02:27.081
The answer: Fixed.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.626
Question 2.

00:02:29.626 --> 00:02:31.271
An inverted curve suggests?

00:02:35.691 --> 00:02:38.386
The answer: The market expects rates to fall.

00:02:39.686 --> 00:02:40.956
Question 3.

00:02:40.956 --> 00:02:43.031
You think borrow rates will spike.

00:02:43.031 --> 00:02:44.376
How do you protect a loan?

00:02:48.796 --> 00:02:51.151
The answer: Switch to fixed-rate borrowing.

00:02:52.451 --> 00:02:53.696
Let's recap.

00:02:53.696 --> 00:02:56.729
Floating rates: lending and borrowing APYs

00:02:56.729 --> 00:02:59.851
that change with utilisation (Module 3).

00:02:59.851 --> 00:03:03.241
Fixed rates: PTs (10.1), fixed-rate lending

00:03:03.241 --> 00:03:06.546
markets and fixed-rate borrowing (#22).

00:03:06.546 --> 00:03:11.065
Term structure: PT implied yields across maturities form

00:03:11.065 --> 00:03:14.616
a yield curve (e.g. 3-month vs 12-month).

00:03:14.616 --> 00:03:17.671
Positioning: buying PT = receiving a fixed

00:03:17.671 --> 00:03:20.371
rate (you win if floating rates fall).

00:03:21.671 --> 00:03:24.186
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:24.186 --> 00:03:28.246
Next up, Lesson 10.9: Peg and redemption arbitrage.
